 "description": "A juvenile Belatz: 2 body regions (B2), a head, 2 eyes, a 2-leaf crest, 2 legs, 2 flaps, a tail; feathers; upright, neck head. Coat: colour cobalt; fluff between; sheen between; feathers between; fur reach body only; second colour butter. Face: head large; beak long; crest tall; crown tall; eyes huge. Shape: waist thin; back line dipping; hind body small; body egg; build slim. Legs & tail: tail curl hangs; tail short, thin. Proportions: a large body, a big head, the head carried high, a long beak, a tall crest, a tall feather crest, long legs, broad feet, a thin waist, a dipping back, a short tail, the tail hanging, wide flaps, a slim build.",
